          "case_name": "Wood v. State, Department of Health & Welfare",
          "citation": "127 Idaho 513, 903 P.2d 102 (Ct. App. 1995)",
          "court": "Idaho Court of Appeals",
          "year": 1995,
          "date_decided": "1995-06-15",
          "holding": "The court affirmed an order placing three children in permanent foster care until age eighteen, holding that a magistrate need not make a threshold determination limiting the CASA guardian ad litem's participation because I.C. § 16-1632(a) gives the guardian ad litem all the rights of a party, and that any evidentiary error was harmless.",
          "relevance": "The permanency order ran until the children reached eighteen, marking the statutory horizon of CPA foster care.",
          "quote": "which vests the guardian ad litem with all the rights of a party to a lawsuit",
          "url": "https://www.courtlistener.com/opinion/5341701/wood-v-state-department-of-health-welfare/",
          "courtlistener_cluster_id": 5341701
        },
        {
          "case_name": "Idaho Department of Health & Welfare v. John Doe (2023-25)",
          "citation": "No. 50875 (Idaho Nov. 3, 2023)",
          "court": "Idaho Supreme Court",
          "year": 2023,
          "date_decided": "2023-11-03",
          "holding": "Affirming a redisposition order removing five children from a home that had been under protective supervision, the court held for the first time that a redisposition hearing under I.C. § 16-1623 is governed by the same preponderance-of-the-evidence standard as an adjudicatory hearing and does not unconstitutionally interfere with parental rights.",
          "relevance": "Notes that protective supervision may run for an indeterminate period not to exceed the child's eighteenth birthday.",
          "quote": "The redisposition hearing process is, in essence, another adjudicatory hearing resulting in a \"redisposition\" of the child's custody",
          "url": "https://www.courtlistener.com/opinion/9437138/idhw-v-john-doe/",
          "courtlistener_cluster_id": 9437138
        }
